From 70732251021529702cafa0268f36e9aadf444a45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:53:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 063/108] gpu: skip ownership transfers a full-rectangle clear
 overwrites; feed fully-resolved textures; sync diagnostics

- gpu_skip_overwritten_transfers (default 0 for now): when the draw that needs
  an ownership transfer into a depth render target is a single screen-space
  rectangle (rectangle list, quad list or 4-vertex strip) writing depth with
  ALWAYS, with no alpha test / alpha-to-mask / pixel kill and a full MSAA
  sample mask, the rectangle it covers is cut out of the transfer (reusing the
  resolve-clear cut-out). 1 = only if the stencil is replaced as well, 2 = also
  when the stencil isn't written. Lightning Returns clears its shadow-map
  cascades and its 4x "clear trick" target this way. The rectangle comes from
  DrawExtentEstimator::EstimateRectangleCoverage (vertex shader on the CPU,
  rectangle lists completed via the longest edge as Xenia expands them,
  clipped draws limited to the viewport and to depth inside the clip volume).
- Resolve feed: a resolve covering the whole single-level texture feeds it
  even if it was already outdated.
- Diagnostics (off): gpu_log_transfer_draws now prints why no cut-out was made;
  vulkan_resolve_full_barrier_before_copy, vulkan_rt_barrier_new_pass,
  vulkan_submission_start_full_barrier.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

